 R←Test_API_029(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;tempDir;rc;msg;qdmx
⍝ Runs "GetMainOrMaster" on a project with "main", with both "main" and "master", and with neither.
⍝ The result of ⍸ used to be handed to ⊃ as a PATH, so with both branches present the function
⍝ returned a single character, and with neither it returned both names.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 tempDir←FilesAndDirs.GetTempSubDir'APLGit2-',⊃⎕SI
 (##.CiderConfig.HOME,'/TestData/CiderProject4.zip')ZipArchive.UnzipTo tempDir
 →T.GoToTidyUp'main'≢G.GetMainOrMaster tempDir

 ⍝ Both of them: "main" wins
 {}tempDir G.U.RunGitCommand'branch master'
 →T.GoToTidyUp'main'≢G.GetMainOrMaster tempDir

 ⍝ Only "master" is left
 {}tempDir G.U.RunGitCommand'checkout -q master'
 {}tempDir G.U.RunGitCommand'branch -D main'
 →T.GoToTidyUp'master'≢G.GetMainOrMaster tempDir

 ⍝ Neither: an error rather than a wrong answer
 {}tempDir G.U.RunGitCommand'checkout -q -b dev'
 {}tempDir G.U.RunGitCommand'branch -D master'
 :Trap 0
     {}G.GetMainOrMaster tempDir
     →T.GoToTidyUp 1
 :Else
     qdmx←⎕DMX
     →T.GoToTidyUp~∨/'Neither a "main"'⍷qdmx.EM,qdmx.Message
 :EndTrap

 R←T._OK

∆TidyUp:
 (rc msg)←FilesAndDirs.RmDirByForce tempDir
 msg Assert rc=0
⍝Done
